[/asy]

What is the exact value of $v(-1.5) + v(0) + v(1.5)$ ?

Four. (15 points) As shown in Figure 3, in the Cartesian coordinate system $x O y$, $\odot O: x^{2}+y^{2}=4$ intersects the positive half-axis of the $x$-axis at point $A$, $\odot A:(x-2)^{2}+y^{2}=r^{2}(r>0)$ intersects $\odot O$ at points $B$ and $C$.
(1) Find the minimum value of $\overrightarrow{A B} \cdot \overrightarrow{A C}$;
(2) Let $P$ be any point on $\odot O$ other than $B$ and $C$, and let the lines $P B$ and $P C$ intersect the $x$-axis at points $M$ and $N$, respectively. Find the maximum value of $S_{\triangle P O M} S_{\triangle P O N}$.

In rectangle $ABCD$, side $AB$ measures $8$ units and side $BC$ measures $4$ units, as shown. Points $F$ and $G$ are on side $CD$ with segment $DF$ measuring $2$ units and segment $GC$ measuring $3$ units, and lines $AF$ and $BG$ intersect at $E$. Determine the area of triangle $AEB$. [asy]
draw((0,0)--(8,0)--(8,4)--(0,4)--cycle);
draw((0,0)--(3,8)--(8,0)--cycle);
dot((0,0));
dot((8,0));
dot((8,4));
dot((0,4));
dot((2,4));
dot((5,4));
dot((3,8));
label("A",(0,0),SW);
label("B",(8,0),SE);
label("C",(8,4),NE);
label("D",(0,4),NW);
label("E",(3,8),N);
label("F",(2,4),SE);
label("G",(5,4),SW);
label("8",(4,0),S);
label("2",(1,4),N);
label("3",(6.5,4),N);
label("4",(8,2),E);
[/asy]

Define the sequences $(a_n),(b_n)$ by
\begin{align*}
& a_n, b_n > 0, \forall n\in\mathbb{N_+} \\ 
& a_{n+1} = a_n - \frac{1}{1+\sum_{i=1}^n\frac{1}{a_i}} \\ 
& b_{n+1} = b_n + \frac{1}{1+\sum_{i=1}^n\frac{1}{b_i}}
\end{align*}
1) If $a_{100}b_{100} = a_{101}b_{101}$, find the value of $a_1-b_1$;
2) If $a_{100} = b_{99}$, determine which is larger between $a_{100}+b_{100}$ and $a_{101}+b_{101}$.

Calculate the value of the following expressions:  
(1) $(0.25)^{-2}+8^{ \frac {2}{3}}-416^{3}+2^{log_{2}3}$;  
(2) $\lg 16+3\lg 5-\lg \frac {1}{5}+\log_{2}9\cdot \log_{3}4$.

A function $g$ from the integers to the integers is defined as:
\[g(n) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
n + 5 & \text{if $n$ is odd}, \\
n/2 & \text{if $n$ is even}.
\end{array}
\right.\]
Suppose $m$ is odd and $g(g(g(m))) = 35.$ Find $m$.

Given that the equation of ellipse $C$ is $\frac{x^{2}}{a^{2}} + \frac{y^{2}}{b^{2}} = 1 (a > b > 0)$, the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\frac{x^{2}}{a^{2}} - \frac{y^{2}}{b^{2}} = 1$ are $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, and the angle between $l_{1}$ and the $x$-axis is $30^{\circ}$, and the focal length of the hyperbola is $4 \sqrt{2}$.
(1) Find the equation of ellipse $C$;
(2) A line $l$ passing through the right focus $F$ of ellipse $C$ intersects ellipse $C$ at points $A$ and $B$, and circle $O$: $x^{2} + y^{2} = a^{2}$ at points $D$ and $E$. When the area of triangle $OAB$ is maximum, find the length of chord $DE$.
